# Mayhem target `splitlen` — the hashcat-utils `splitlen` command-line tool, one of the package's public
# utilities (src/Makefile `native:`), built sanitized (ASan+UBSan, halting) + SanCov + DWARF-3 by
# mayhem/build.sh at /mayhem/cli/splitlen. Raw (non-libFuzzer, process-per-input) target:
# `splitlen outdir < infile` — reads words on stdin; the 64 per-length output files go under /tmp (an absolute tmpfs path is sanctioned by SPEC §6.2 item 13). Run #1 wrote them into the working directory and Mayhem's own runner (mayhem-fuzz) fell into a restart loop there, so the output is kept out of the cwd. No `@@`, so Mayhem delivers the fuzz bytes on stdin.
# A slow or hanging input is bounded by Mayhem's own per-test limit, the explicit 5 s `timeout:` below (no in-process watchdog).
project: savantenvs/hashcat-utils
target: splitlen

testsuite:
  - https://$MAYHEM_DOMAIN/$MAYHEM_PROJECT/$MAYHEM_TARGET/testsuite.tar
  - file://mayhem/splitlen/testsuite

cmds:
  - cmd: /mayhem/cli/splitlen /tmp
    timeout: 5
